<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4657] Cache entry eviction can be broken if store throws exception</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4657</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Fix for &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4465&quot; title=&quot;Read-through is not properly working with multiple gets executed in parallel&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-4465&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-4465&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (commit 22b7e76c00a77a06388bcef869f29d1a572a306a) introduced cache entry &apos;reservation&apos; while entry is loaded from store. When entry is reserved it is not evicted from cache. But currently &apos;reserved&apos; status is not cleared when cache store&apos;s methods throw exception, this should be fixed in GridcCacheAdaptergetAllAsync0: catch exception thrown from ctx.store().loadAll and do required cleanup.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
